# Architecture Outcome

The Physical Persistence Model becomes the authoritative physical representation of enterprise information across HCGO.

It faithfully represents:

- Constitutional Governance
- Enterprise Discovery
- Enterprise Analysis
- Enterprise Persistence Architecture
- Enterprise Conceptual Information Model
- Enterprise Logical Information Model

All subsequent Technology Implementations—including PostgreSQL and future persistence technologies—shall faithfully implement the Physical Persistence Model.

No Technology Implementation may redefine:

- Enterprise Semantics
- Conceptual Representation
- Logical Organization
- Physical Representation
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Governance
- Enterprise Traceability
- Enterprise Lifecycle Authority

established by earlier architectural phases.

The Physical Persistence Model therefore serves as the authoritative bridge between Persistence Architecture and Technology Implementation.

---

# Current Assessment

The Physical Persistence Model establishes the authoritative physical representation of enterprise information across HCGO.

It faithfully represents previously validated enterprise semantics through technology-independent physical persistence structures while preserving enterprise authority, ownership, stewardship, governance, traceability, lifecycle authority, and logical organization.

Technology implementation becomes subordinate to the completed architecture.

Every persistence technology shall faithfully implement the Physical Persistence Model without redefining enterprise semantics established through Constitutional Governance, Enterprise Discovery, Enterprise Analysis, Enterprise Persistence Architecture, the Enterprise Conceptual Information Model, or the Enterprise Logical Information Model.

This preserves complete architectural traceability from Constitutional Governance through final technology implementation.